# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/np1-fastlane window (the lone-user padded round; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/np1-fastlane and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-np1-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-np1-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the same
# in every serving job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone.
# A1 (EXACTNESS of the lone-user padded round, STOP): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-np1-audit, the ship-4 audited twin (every audit of the candidate:
# the K/V page writer's audit of every unit it writes, the verify T2 audit, the pre-stage diff and two-block pre-stage audits, the multi-user SDPA launch's audit, the
# vglue, conv-gates and octo-lever audits, the host tier, the host read-backs SAMPLED) with QWEN_FAST_SOLO_PACKED=1, on Swift. The flag adds ONE block to the KV cache
# tensors (a scratch page past vLLM's pool) and lets a lone live user (and a lone user of the other block) take the padded 64-row round with its third idle segment on that
# page. warmup; coding (ONE user for 1,500 tokens: every round a lone-user padded round, the audited ones compare the served composition with the sequential one on the idle
# segments too); np1_live2 (a pair: two idle segments, page 0 alone, the flag changes nothing); concurrent5_split (four users in block A and a fifth ALONE in block B, then
# a sixth: the split the placement leaves); concurrent8_drain (eight users whose budgets end one by one: every live count from 8 to 1, every split of the two blocks);
# concurrent8_steady (the octo rounds, required by the smoke check on this profile). READ: octo_judge.py --container-log <container log> --profile
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-np1-audit clean (the solo rule: at least one "packed padded round live=1" line, no "packed padded skipped live=1
# eligible=1" line, beside the octo rules); the NP1 lines in the container log: "[NP1] kv scratch: Qwen36ForCausalLM.allocate_kv_cache allocates 1 block(s) beyond the pool
# vLLM sized (pool 16500 blocks, scratch ids 16500..16500)" once, "[SOLO-PACKED] admitted min_users=1 scratch_pages=16500 (gate only)" once and, for each of the two M3
# blocks, "packed padded block admitted min_users=1 users=4 max_idle=4 ... scratch_pages=16500"; the octo block's own admitted line is unchanged (min_users=6, max_idle=2,
# no scratch pages); every audit line exact=True with entries above 0, in particular the K/V page writer's audit on a round with idle=[...] of three segments (the unit that
# writes the scratch page); NO "audit mismatch", NO "fell back", NO "kv shared", NO "page0 ... refused" for an eligible lone user, no stall. The memory ledger's free DRAM
# per chip after the attach: RECORD it (the scratch page is 557,056 bytes a chip). ANY failure is NO-GO for the lone-user round and halts the window. CHECKPOINT READ (the
# workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache W0 of the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the
# models answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second
# through the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks,
# not the lever. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED. Duration (estimate): 120 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-np1-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-np1-audit
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,np1_live2,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain,concurrent8_steady
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=180
